### Search result for gaps in current physics carriers

I searched only the current canonical **physics/items**, **physics/library**, root **items**, and root **library**, not archived runs. The physics QFT category contains local free/QED models and mathematics pages above, but I found no current physics item/page that defines a general physical \(p\)-form or higher-group symmetry, realizes noninvertible QFT defect fusion, proves a global anomaly under large gauge transformations, or classifies spin/higher categorical anomalies. The current QED local-coupling postulate explicitly excludes large gauge transformations and nontrivial bundles. This is a gap in local authoring/coverage, not evidence that established mathematics or physics results remain unproved in the literature.

